**# Frontend principles**

**## SOLID**

- UI = presentation only; no business rules duplicated from Postgres.

- Data via Supabase client / hooks / server components; views and RPC as in `docs/HANDOFF.md`.

- Do not add Express/Nest/Prisma or a second API layer.

- Role checks in Next.js middleware and layout guards — not scattered across 20 pages.

**## DRY**

- Reuse shadcn/ui primitives; shared `app/` layouts for client vs staff.

- Types from Supabase generated `Database` types — do not hand-copy table shapes.

- Staff tables (admin, picker, courier): one `DataTable` wrapper + column configs per screen.

**## KISS**

- No Redux/Zustand unless a concrete cross-page state need appears.

- MVP stubs from HANDOFF: payment → `paid`, SMS, like — minimal UI, no extra services.

- Prefer server components + one client boundary per feature.

**## UI-kit**

- **Source of truth:** Figma Green — [https://www.figma.com/design/rzkHWJsXsgN36q3P8mrkAA/Green](https://www.figma.com/design/rzkHWJsXsgN36q3P8mrkAA/Green)

- Screen list: `docs/screens.md`

- Stack: Tailwind + shadcn/ui; tokens aligned with design (no random hex).

- Icons: Iconify / Majesticons as in design.

- Fonts: Evolventa + Inter — load once in root layout.

- Do not invent one-off components if shadcn or an existing project component fits.

- Before new UI, check Figma frame name in `screens.md`.